Subject: [PATCH] Docs: second review of the backend/frontend redesign (round
 2, 12 new findings)

Adds docs/design/backend/08-review-2026-10-02.md. Re-ran all round-1
reproductions against 5b7724f (17 findings: 12 fixed, the rest mostly fixed,
one open by design), then reviewed the ~10.6k new lines.

New findings, most important first: a run that finished while the server was
down is recorded failed with 0/100 (reconcile ignores the progress file that
adoption trusts); the upload handler blocks the event loop and holds ~2x the
file in RAM; SSE coalescing treats per-node graph deltas as supersedable (6
sent, 1 delivered); the dataset file endpoint serves any file in the dataset
dir (db, shards, svg) without hardening headers; the run-detail page
re-introduces the resync / non-finite / silent-catch defects.

Also: rules for contributors, and 12 code-quality recommendations (quality
gate with ruff+mypy, supervisor abstraction, event contract with sequence
numbers, parse-at-boundary, process isolation for graph training, frontend
shared core, contract tests for fakes, resource budgets, ADRs, mutation
testing).

Docs only. Linked from docs/design/backend/README.md.
